#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.p:1229-6
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This guide is primarily designed for color screens. If you are using it "
#| "for the first time, we highly recommend reading this on a computer, "
#| "tablet or mobile. Because seeing user interface elements highlighted in "
#| "color will make your life easier while learning how to use KOReader. Of "
#| "course you can read this on your e-ink device too, but the experience "
#| "will not be optimal."
msgid ""
"This guide is primarily designed for color screens. Especially if you are "
"using it for the first time, we highly recommend reading this on a computer, "
"tablet or a mobile phone instead of a black and white e-ink screen. Seeing "
"different categories of text properly will make your life easier while "
"learning how to use KOReader. Of course you can read this on your e-ink "
"device too, but the experience will not be optimal."
msgstr ""
"Ten przewodnik jest przeznaczony głównie dla ekranów kolorowych. Jeśli "
"korzystasz z niego po raz pierwszy, zdecydowanie zalecamy czytanie go na "
"komputerze, tablecie lub telefonie komórkowym. Wyświetlanie elementów "
"interfejsu użytkownika wyróżnionych kolorem ułatwi Ci naukę korzystania z "
"KOReadera. Oczywiście możesz go czytać również na urządzeniu z czytnikiem e-"
"ink, ale nie będzie to optymalne."

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.p:1231-6
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "You can use the search function of your browser to find a specific topic "
#| "or keyword (generally <b>Ctrl + F</b>). If you have a suggestion or "
#| "question related to this user guide, you can write to this <a "
#| "href=\"https://github.com/koreader/koreader/issues/11147\">GitHub "
#| "discussion thread</a>."
msgid ""
"You can use the search function of your browser to find a specific topic or "
"keyword (generally <b>Ctrl + F</b>). If you have a suggestion, correction or "
"question related to this user guide, you can write to this <a href=\"https://"
"github.com/koreader/koreader/issues/11147\">GitHub discussion thread</a>."
