#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.div:5153-6
msgctxt "user_guide/en.html:L2-optimizing"
msgid "9.4 Optimizing Documents"
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.p:5155-6
msgid ""
"KOReader is designed to work efficiently even on the limited hardware of e-"
"book readers. But there will always be poorly formatted documents which slow "
"down KOReader. Here we will give some tips for optimizing your document "
"depending on the file type."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.div:5159-6
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Profiles"
msgid "EPUB files"
msgstr "Profile"

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ul.li:5162-7
msgid ""
"EPUB files are basically composed of text and images with some rules to "
"determine how these items are formatted on the screen. In ideal conditions, "
"this is a fairly simple process so EPUB files are generally fast in "
"KOReader. <b>But some EPUB books add a great number of formatting rules that "
"KOReader has to do many calculations just to show even a single sentence.</"
"b> This will slow down opening the book, turning the pages and changing the "
"appearance properties like font weight or line spacing."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ul.li.div:5165-8
msgid ""
"<span class=\"microns_info\" title=\"Contextual information\"></span> "
"KOReader doesn't support <b>fixed layout EPUBs</b>. They will open, but will "
"render as reflowable EPUBs and probably won't look nice or readable."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ul.li:5168-7
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "<span class=\"label_blue\">INFO</span> Partial rendering is only possible "
#| "if your EPUB is composed of multiple fragments. EPUB files are "
#| "basically .zip archives that contain .html files. Some books can be a "
#| "single .html file while others may be composed of multiple .html files "
#| "like each chapter of the book is a separate .html file. <b>If your book "
#| "is only a single .html file, partial rendering can not work, because for "
#| "each change KOReader still has to calculate the whole book.</b>"
msgid ""
"EPUB files are actually ZIP archives that contain HTML files. Some books can "
"be a single HTML file while others may be composed of multiple HTML files "
"like each chapter of the book is a separate HTML file. <b>If your book is "
"only a single HTML file, partial rendering can not work.</b> So appearance "
"changes will be slower than the divided chapter books, because for each "
"change, KOReader still has to calculate the whole book instead of only the "
"current chapter."
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"label_blue\">INFO</span>Częściowe załadowanie jest możliwe "
"tylko, gdy EPUB jest złożony z kilku fragmentów. Pliki EPUB są właściwie "
"archiwami .zip, które zawierają pliki .html. Niektóre książki mogą być "
"pojedynczym plikiem .html, a inne mogą być złożone z kilku plików .html jak "
"np. każdy rozdział książki jest oddzielnym plikiem .html.<b>Jeśli twoja "
"książka jest pojedynczym plikiem .html, częściowe renderowanie może nie "
"zadziałać, ponieważ dla każdej zmiany KOReader nadal musi wykonać obliczenia "
"dla całej książki.</b>"

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ul.li:5171-7
msgid ""
"Another rare case of slowness is when the content is wrapped in a <b>HTML "
"table tag</b>. KOReader has to render/draw each cell on each page turn, so "
"if a cell (containing many paragraphs) spans 50 pages, this will make page "
"turning quite slow."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.p:5174-6
#, fuzzy
msgid "Solutions:"
msgstr "Kolekcje"

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ul.li:5177-7
msgid ""
"You can set <span class=\"ui\">Embedded Styles</span> to <b>OFF</b> in the "
"bottom menu to see if ignoring all the document stylesheets makes it faster "
"(of course, you'll probably lose any nice formatting, but you'll know what "
"is the culprit)."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ul.li:5181-7
msgid ""
"If you have HTML and CSS knowledge, you can inspect the HTML and the CSS "
"files directly from KOReader and judge their quality or unnecessary "
"complexity by yourself. To do this, you can long-press on some text and "
"choose <span class=\"ui\">View HTML</span> in the popup menu."
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ul.li:5184-7
msgid ""
"If you have the <b>“content wrapped in a table”</b> problem as mentioned "
"above in the problems section, you can add this <span class=\"ui\">table, "
"tr, td { display:block; }</span> book-specific style tweak to:"
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ul.li.div:5188-8
msgid ""
"TOP MENU / <img class=\"img_inline\" src=\"pictures/top_document.svg\" "
"style=\"width:22px;\"> / Style tweaks / Book-specific tweak"
msgstr ""

#: user_guide/en.html%2Bhtml.body.div.main.div.section.ul.li:5191-7
msgid ""
"<span class=\"external\">Calibre</span>’s e-book editor can check EPUB files "
"for problems and has tools to fix some of the problems."
msgstr ""

